.SS batch
Bounded JSONL batches of the supported read and readiness operations with persisted per\-item recovery.
.TP
.B samedaydesk batch run \-\-input\-file <string> [\-\-state\-dir <string>] [\-\-concurrency <integer>] [\-\-max\-items <integer>] [\-\-max\-line\-bytes <integer>] [\-\-timeout\-ms <integer>] [\-\-credential\-file <string>] [\-\-credential\-stdin] [\-\-origin <string>] [\-\-allow\-loopback] [\-\-dry\-run]
Run a JSONL batch of supported reads. One JSONL record per item plus start and summary records; per\-item state persisted before dispatch; rerun skips completed items. Effect: read. Auth: optional_tenant. Retry: bounded_get per item; no POST. Recovery: rerun with the same \-\-state\-dir: completed items are skipped with their archived result, changed terms for an existing id are refused, unconfirmed reads are rerun.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-input\-file
JSONL items file, or \- for stdin. Each line: {"id"?: string, "op": string, "args"?: object}. Required.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-state\-dir
Absolute 0700 directory for per\-item recovery state and archived results. Required unless \-\-dry\-run. Reuse it to resume.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-concurrency
Items in flight. Default 4, hard cap 8.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-max\-items
Refuse input past this many items. Default 1000, hard cap 10000.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-max\-line\-bytes
Refuse a longer input line. Default 16384, hard cap 65536.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-timeout\-ms
Per\-item deadline, reported as request_timeout. Default 15000.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-credential\-file
Absolute path to an existing 0600 tenant credential file. The value is never printed.
.RE
.RS
