.SH SIGNALS
SIGINT aborts an in\-flight request where client\-io supports AbortSignal, prints a cancelled error envelope (or, in batch run, cancelled item records and a summary) and exits 130. Remote work already sent is not cancelled. A closed stdout (EPIPE) in batch run stops dispatch, persists state and exits 14.
